CAT = "zapsiraSafety"; SEG = "OHS"
# Occupational Health and Safety Act 85 of 1993 (gov.za copy): ss. 8, 14, 15, 17; general
# workplace safety for security officers.
Q = [
("Which Act sets general health and safety duties in South African workplaces?",
 "The OHS Act", ["The Criminal Procedure Act", "The Road Accident Fund Act", "The Consumer Protection Act"],
 "The Occupational Health and Safety Act 85 of 1993 sets the duties of employers and employees to keep workplaces safe."),
("Under section 14 of the Occupational Health and Safety Act, what must every employee take reasonable care of?",
 "Own and others' safety", ["Only the client's property", "Only their own uniform", "Only the company vehicle"],
 "Section 14(a) requires every employee to take reasonable care for their own health and safety and that of others affected by their acts or omissions."),
("A guard is injured in an incident at work. By when must the guard report it under section 14?",
 "By the end of that shift", ["Within one month", "Only if off work for a week", "At the next annual review"],
 "Section 14(e) requires an employee to report an incident that caused injury as soon as practicable, and not later than the end of the shift in which it happened, unless that was impossible."),
("A guard sees an unsafe situation, such as exposed live wires near the gate. What does section 14 require?",
 "Report it promptly", ["Fix the wires personally", "Ignore it, it is not security", "Report it at month end"],
 "Section 14(d) requires an employee to report any unsafe or unhealthy situation to the employer or health and safety representative as soon as practicable."),
("What does section 15 of the Act forbid?",
 "Misusing safety equipment", ["Wearing a uniform", "Working the night shift", "Using a two-way radio"],
 "Section 15 says no person may intentionally or recklessly interfere with, damage or misuse anything provided in the interest of health or safety, such as an extinguisher."),
("Under section 8 of the Act, what must the employer provide and maintain?",
 "A safe workplace", ["Pay for employees' cars", "Choose employees' meals", "Supply home security"],
 "Section 8 requires the employer to provide and maintain, as far as reasonably practicable, a working environment that is safe and without risk to health."),
("An employer has more than 20 employees at a workplace. What must the employer designate under section 17?",
 "Safety representatives", ["A company lawyer", "A union shop steward", "A first aid sponsor"],
 "Section 17 requires an employer with more than 20 employees at a workplace to designate health and safety representatives in writing."),
("Why must a guard follow lawful safety rules given by the employer?",
 "Section 14 requires it", ["Only if the guard agrees", "Only on day shift", "Only if a client is watching"],
 "Section 14(c) requires employees to carry out lawful orders and obey the health and safety rules and procedures laid down by the employer."),
("A guard working at a construction site is given a hard hat and safety boots. When must they be worn?",
 "Whenever site rules say", ["Only when it rains", "Only when inspectors visit", "Only on the first day"],
 "Personal protective equipment protects only when it is worn. Follow the site's PPE rules throughout the shift."),
("A guard on a long standing post at the gate starts to feel back pain. What is a sensible step?",
 "Vary posture, report it", ["Ignore it until it is bad", "Sit on the boom gate", "Leave the post to rest"],
 "Changing position and reporting ongoing discomfort lets the employer adjust the post, for example with a chair or mat."),
("A guard on night patrol must cross a wet, poorly lit floor. What is the main hazard?",
 "A slip or fall", ["Sunburn", "Noise damage", "Dehydration"],
 "Wet floors and poor lighting cause slips and falls. Use a torch, walk carefully and report the hazard."),
("A guard on an outdoor post in summer heat starts feeling dizzy and has a headache. What should be done?",
 "Rest in shade, drink water", ["Keep working without a break", "Drink an energy drink only", "Run to warm up"],
 "Dizziness and headache in heat can be early heat exhaustion. Rest in shade, drink water and report it; get medical help if it worsens."),
("Why should a guard not lift a heavy box using the back alone?",
 "It risks back injury", ["It makes the box dirty", "It is slower", "It uses less energy"],
 "Bend the knees, keep the load close and lift with the legs, or get help. Poor lifting is a common cause of back injury."),
("A guard on night shift feels very tired on the drive home. What is the safest choice?",
 "Rest before driving", ["Drive faster to get home", "Open the window and push on", "Drink alcohol to relax"],
 "Fatigue slows reactions like alcohol does. Rest first or use other transport if too tired to drive safely."),
("Which item of equipment helps a guard be seen by drivers at a gate at night?",
 "A reflective vest", ["Dark sunglasses", "A black jacket", "A cap with no badge"],
 "High-visibility, reflective clothing makes a guard visible in vehicle headlights and reduces the risk of being struck."),
("A guard is told to check a fenced area where a sign warns of electrified fencing. What should the guard do?",
 "Keep clear of it", ["Touch it to test it", "Climb it to save time", "Cut it to get through"],
 "Electric fences can cause serious injury. Keep away and follow the site's procedure for faults or alarms on the fence."),
("A dog on the client's site is aggressive and not under control. What should the guard do?",
 "Avoid it and report it", ["Chase it off with a stick", "Feed it to calm it", "Ignore the danger"],
 "An uncontrolled animal is a hazard. Keep a safe distance and report it so the owner or the right service can deal with it."),
("What should a guard do with a first aid box that is missing items?",
 "Report it for restocking", ["Leave it as it is", "Take items home", "Throw the box away"],
 "First aid boxes must be kept stocked. Report shortages so the employer can replace them before they are needed."),
("A guard is asked to stand in a busy delivery yard without any traffic plan. What is the main risk?",
 "Being hit by a vehicle", ["Getting sunburnt only", "Losing the radio", "Missing a meal break"],
 "Reversing trucks and forklifts are a serious hazard. Ask for a safe position and a clear traffic plan, and stay visible."),
("A guard who is ill with a fever is scheduled for duty. What is the responsible choice?",
 "Tell the supervisor early", ["Work and say nothing", "Leave the post halfway without telling", "Send a friend in your place"],
 "Telling the supervisor early lets a registered relief be arranged. Sending an unregistered person in your place is not allowed."),
]
